{
  "requirement": "In the rationale of each changed record, `habeas refactor` MUST rewrite each\ncode span that is exactly `<file>#<selector>` for a mapped node, or for a node\nin a mapped file, to the node's new address.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests are adequate for `requirements.refactor.rationale.addresses`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. A code span that is exactly `<file>#<selector>` for a node with a node mapping is rewritten to that node's new address.\n2. A code span that is exactly `<file>#<selector>` for a node in a path-mapped file is rewritten to the node's new address. The selector is kept and the file part is remapped.\n3. The rewriting applies in the rationale of each changed record.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `src/refactor/tests.rs#fn[rationales_rewrite_exact_code_spans_and_list_other_mentions]` covers obligation 1.\n  - It uses a node mapping `src/a.rs#fn[f]` to `src/b.rs#fn[f]`.\n  - It asserts that the span `` `src/a.rs#fn[f]` `` becomes `` `src/b.rs#fn[f]` `` inside a full-string `assert_eq!`.\n  - The same assertion shows that near-miss spans are not wrongly rewritten: the bare `src/a.rs` root, `src/a.rs:3`, and `see src/old/x.rs`.\n- `src/refactor/tests.rs#fn[rationales_rewrite_addresses_of_nodes_in_mapped_files]` covers obligation 2.\n  - It uses the path mapping `src/old` to `src/new`.\n  - It asserts that `` `src/old/x.rs#fn[f]` `` and the nested selector `` `src/old/x.rs#mod[m]/fn[g]` `` are rewritten to `src/new/x.rs#…` with the selectors preserved.\n  - It also asserts that no mentions are reported.\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_function_keeps_its_evidence_current]` covers obligation 3 end to end.\n  - `habeas refactor --map src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` changes the record `evidence/rules.load.json`.\n  - The test asserts that the stored rationale now contains `` `src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` ``.\n  - It also asserts that the unrelated `` `src/config.rs` `` span is left alone and reported for review.\n  - A second run changes 0 records.\n\n**Gaps considered**\n- I read `fn[rewrite_rationale]` and `Mappings::node` in `src/refactor.rs` only to understand which scenarios exist. A node mapping applies to the node's descendants, and a node mapping takes precedence over a file path mapping. The requirement text names neither case, so I don't treat either as a gap.\n- Both required classes (mapped node and node in a mapped file) are exercised with exact-output assertions. The tests would catch an implementation that did not rewrite addresses, rewrote only the file part, or dropped the selector.",
